            <ArticleTitle>Persistent urinary retention after tension-free vaginal tape: a new surgical solution.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>95-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The most common post-operative problems seen with the tension-free vaginal tape (TVT) are voiding difficulties. A small subset of patients develops persistent urinary retention, often associated with vaginal pain and dyspareunia. We describe a surgical solution to these complications that involves cutting of the prolene sling just below the urethra and individualised prologation with an additional piece of prolene-mesh.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
